# Sub-1GHz RF transceiver drivers configuration
#

menuconfig SUB1G
	tristate "Sub-1GHz RF transceivers"
	depends on SPI
	help
	  This section contains drivers for Sub-1GHz RF transceivers that
	  operate in the ISM bands below 1GHz (typically 433MHz, 868MHz,
	  915MHz, etc.). These devices are commonly used for low-power
	  wireless applications such as IoT, sensor networks, smart home
	  devices, and industrial automation.

	  If unsure, say N.

if SUB1G

config CMT2300A
	tristate "CMOSTEK CMT2300A Sub-GHz RF transceiver"
	depends on SPI
	select GPIOLIB
	help
	  This driver supports the CMOSTEK CMT2300A Sub-GHz RF transceiver.
	  The CMT2300A is a highly integrated sub-GHz RF transceiver designed
	  for low power wireless applications in the sub-1GHz ISM bands.
	  It supports OOK, FSK, and GFSK modulation schemes.

	  The driver provides a character device interface (/dev/sub1g_dev*)
	  for userspace applications to interact with the transceiver for
	  transmitting and receiving data.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called cmt2300a.

	  If unsure, say N.

endif # SUB1G
